{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>When YHWH your Elohim gives rest.</b> The reason is that this commandment depends on [their] having inherited the land and the land being at rest from war on all its surroundings, for as long as they are engaged in wars with those near them, they are not obligated to fight Amalek." "<b>You shall blot out the memory of Amalek.</b> This is [the meaning of] 'and you shall strike, from man to woman, from infant to suckling, from ox to sheep' — so that no one will say, 'This ox was Amalek's spoil.' The words of the Torah are general; the words of Samuel the prophet are specific." "<b>You shall not forget.</b> After 'remember,' for emphasis. And so is the manner of many commandments in the Torah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:53.023574466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}